jean-luc godard changed how we write and  direct he changed how we shoot and edit  he changed how we use music and sound  even title cards he didn't just break  the rules he he ran him over in a stolen  car and then threw it in reverse and  backed over them to make sure they were  dead  Godard once said every film should have  a beginning a middle and an end but not  necessarily in that order  and in keeping with that spirit we would  like to propose our toast to him now  even though we're not done with this  tribute  mr. Godard in your long career as a  filmmaker and provocateur let's be  honest you have said things that have  offended pretty much everybody in this  room at least once you have also said  really snarky things about Hollywood and  the Oscars but then again so has  everybody in this room at least once  none of that has deterred this board of  governors from bestowing upon you the  the highest honor we can for artistic  achievement let's be clear this ain't  the Hersholt Humanitarian Award this  someone had to say it of course it's the  writer this is an honorary Oscar I  shouldn't be saying this to me there's  an honorary Oscar for your brilliance  your innovation there you are  and your unapologetic orneriness you  have enriched our artform immeasurably  it's impossible to imagine contemporary  cinema without your influence and for  that and all the great films we say  Thank You mr. Godard wherever you are  you
 

